spans.s:
gaṇá, m.
 —1. troop, (of Maruts) 90^16;
crowd, (of friends) 3^9; host (of stars);
flock, (of birds) 3^8;
 —2. pl. troop-deities,
inferior deities which regularly appear not
singly, but in troops, 67^13; esp. those that
compose the retinue of Śiva; then, as sing.,
a single one of Śiva's attendants, a Gana,
55^20;
 —3. a number.
